Self-belief.

66
00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:48.885
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.272
Visal, were you always a confident student?

68
00:03:53.383 --> 00:03:58.999
No. I used to feel nervous in class. I used to avoid public speaking.

69
00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:01.096
What changed?

70
00:04:02.183 --> 00:04:06.842
I stepped out of my comfort zone and joined the debate club.

71
00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:08.742
And now?

72
00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:14.938
Now I use positive affirmations, and my self-belief is much stronger.

73
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.041
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.800
Grammar focus: used to plus infinitive.

75
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.333
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.585
I used to feel nervous.

77
00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:28.831
She used to hide at the back of the class.

78
00:04:29.717 --> 00:04:32.053
We didn't use to speak English in public.

79
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:39.727
Use 'used to' for past habits that are not true now. In questions and negatives, write 'use to': Did you use to…?

80
00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:43.774
Be careful! Don't say: I use to feel nervous.

81
00:04:45.733 --> 00:04:47.826
Say: I used to feel nervous.

82
00:04:48.126 --> 00:04:51.054
In positive sentences, write 'used to' with a d.

83
00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:54.565
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:56.774
From Shy to Strong.

85
00:04:57.074 --> 00:04:59.817
I used to feel nervous and full of self-doubt.

86
00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:04.110
I used to stay in my comfort zone and say nothing in class.

87
00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.818
Then I joined a public speaking club and practised my body language.

88
00:05:09.833 --> 00:05:13.377
Every morning I said an affirmation to build my self-esteem.

89
00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:17.864
Now I speak with poise, and my self-belief grows every day.

90
00:05:18.967 --> 00:05:22.620
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:23.483 --> 00:05:25.355
I used blank feel nervous.

92
00:05:25.655 --> 00:05:28.728
A, to. B, for. C, of.

93
00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:33.941
The answer is A: to.

94
00:05:35.083 --> 00:05:37.559
Not believing in your own ability is blank.

95
00:05:37.859 --> 00:05:41.895
A, self-doubt. B, poise. C, empowerment.

96
00:05:45.433 --> 00:05:47.352
The answer is A: self-doubt.

97
00:05:48.517 --> 00:05:51.538
A positive sentence you say to yourself is an blank.

98
00:05:51.838 --> 00:05:56.385
A, affirmation. B, assertiveness. C, body language.

99
00:05:59.933 --> 00:06:01.817
The answer is A: affirmation.

100
00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:05.929
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.329
What has helped you build confidence in yourself?

102
00:06:18.117 --> 00:06:19.524
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:19.824 --> 00:06:28.165
I used to be very shy, but practice has helped me. I joined a speaking club, and positive affirmations have built my self-belief.

104
00:06:28.465 --> 00:06:30.326
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:31.217 --> 00:06:35.796
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and used to plus infinitive.

106
00:06:36.096 --> 00:06:39.759
Today's value is self-confidence. Believe in yourself.

107
00:06:40.059 --> 00:06:42.548
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

108
00:06:42.848 --> 00:06:45.791
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

